# Storefront data conventions

## One source of truth for categories

Category slugs must never be hardcoded per file. The homepage grid, the shop filter
pills, `add-piece`, and the finalize modal all have to agree, or filtering silently
breaks. Read categories on the server with `getCategories()` (`lib/queries.ts`) and pass
them down as props — never import a category array from a client component.

New categories are created through the `createCategory` Server Action in `lib/actions.ts`,
which owns the slugification. Call `slugify()` from `lib/categories.ts` only to preview
the slug in the UI; never build a slug by hand at an insert site.

`show_on_homepage` gates the homepage grid only. The shop filter pills list every
category so nothing becomes unreachable.

## Always write the `photos` array

`shop_inventory.photos` is a `text[]` and the shop reads `photos[0]` as the thumbnail.
Writing a scalar `primary_image` instead produces a listing with no image.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
{ primary_image: lastProgressImage }

// ✅ GOOD
{ photos: [lastProgressImage, ...otherAngles] }
```

## Uploads must persist to Supabase Storage

`URL.createObjectURL(file)` returns a blob URL scoped to the current tab. It dies on
reload, so it must never be saved to the database.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — currently in add-piece and current-project
const mockUploadedUrl = imageSrc

// ✅ GOOD
const { data } = await supabase.storage.from('pieces').upload(path, croppedBlob)
const url = supabase.storage.from('pieces').getPublicUrl(data.path).data.publicUrl
```

Upload the **cropped** output from `react-easy-crop`, not the original file. A
non-empty `onCropComplete` handler is required to get the crop area.

## Ordering and visibility

Admin-reorderable lists (categories, reviews, handiworks) use an integer `sort_order`;
always `.order('sort_order')` on read. Sold pieces stay in `shop_inventory` with
`sold = true` rather than being deleted, so they can appear in the sold-pieces strip.
